/**
\page page_stfcscollection StFcsCollection — FCS Event Data Collection

\section fcs_overview Overview

\ref StFcsCollection is the event-level container for all data produced by the
<b>Forward Calorimeter System (FCS)</b> of the STAR experiment (introduced in the
Run 22 era).  The FCS covers forward pseudorapidities 2.5 < η < 4 and consists of:

- Electromagnetic calorimeters (W-Shashlyk ECAL) — North and South
- Hadronic calorimeters (HCAL) — North and South
- Pre-shower scintillator detectors — North and South

For each event the collection stores three tiers of reconstructed objects indexed by
sub-detector ID (see \ref StFcsDetectorId):

| Tier | Class | Accessor |
|---|---|---|
| Raw tower hits | \ref StFcsHit | \ref StFcsCollection::hits() |
| Shower clusters | \ref StFcsCluster | \ref StFcsCollection::clusters() |
| Photon points | \ref StFcsPoint | \ref StFcsCollection::points() |

\section fcs_ownership Object Ownership

\warning This collection <b>owns</b> every \ref StFcsHit, \ref StFcsCluster, and
\ref StFcsPoint it contains.  The internal \c StSPtrVec containers manage memory
automatically. <b>Do not call \c delete</b> on any pointer retrieved from this
collection — doing so causes a double-free.  Conversely, every object passed to an
\c add*() method <b>must</b> be heap-allocated with \c new and must not be owned
anywhere else.

The collection itself is owned by \ref StEvent, which is managed by the
\c St_DataSet/StXRefMain framework.  \c StEvent's destructor is a no-op; the
framework performs the final cleanup.

\section fcs_detids Sub-Detector IDs

All per-detector methods accept an \c unsigned \c int detector index from the
\ref StFcsDetectorId enumeration:

| Constant | Value | Description |
|---|---|---|
| \c kFcsEcalNorthDetId | 0 | ECAL (W-Shashlyk) North |
| \c kFcsEcalSouthDetId | 1 | ECAL South |
| \c kFcsHcalNorthDetId | 2 | HCAL North |
| \c kFcsHcalSouthDetId | 3 | HCAL South |
| \c kFcsPresNorthDetId | 4 | Pre-shower North |
| \c kFcsPresSouthDetId | 5 | Pre-shower South |
| \c kFcsNDet = 6        | 6 | Sentinel / total sub-detector count |

Hit arrays have size \c kFcsNDet+1 (index 6 is a spare for overflow); cluster and
point arrays have size \c kFcsNDet.  Index access is always guarded by a modulo
operation.

\section fcs_datamembers Data Members

| Type | Name | Description |
|---|---|---|
| \c StSPtrVecFcsHit[kFcsNDet+1] | \c mHits | Hit arrays, one per sub-detector. |
| \c StSPtrVecFcsCluster[kFcsNDet] | \c mClusters | Cluster arrays, one per sub-detector. |
| \c StSPtrVecFcsPoint[kFcsNDet] | \c mPoints | Photon-point arrays, one per sub-detector. |
| \c Int_t | \c mFcsReconstructionFlag | Packed reconstruction-algorithm flags. |
| \c Int_t | \c mDataExist | Non-zero if FCS data were present in the DAQ file. |

\section fcs_methods Key Methods

| Method | Description |
|---|---|
| \ref StFcsCollection::addHit "addHit(det, hit)" | Append a hit for sub-detector \a det. |
| \ref StFcsCollection::hits "hits(det)" | Return reference to the hit vector for \a det. |
| \ref StFcsCollection::numberOfHits "numberOfHits(det)" | Number of hits for \a det. |
| \ref StFcsCollection::addCluster "addCluster(det, cl)" | Append a cluster. |
| \ref StFcsCollection::clusters "clusters(det)" | Reference to the cluster vector. |
| \ref StFcsCollection::numberOfClusters "numberOfClusters(det)" | Cluster count. |
| \ref StFcsCollection::addPoint "addPoint(det, pt)" | Append a photon point. |
| \ref StFcsCollection::points "points(det)" | Reference to the point vector. |
| \ref StFcsCollection::numberOfPoints "numberOfPoints(det)" | Point count. |
| \ref StFcsCollection::isDataExist "isDataExist()" | Returns 1 if FCS DAQ data present. |
| \ref StFcsCollection::setDataExist "setDataExist(v)" | Set the DAQ-data-present flag. |
| \ref StFcsCollection::fcsReconstructionFlag "fcsReconstructionFlag()" | Packed flags. |
| \ref StFcsCollection::setFcsReconstructionFlag "setFcsReconstructionFlag(v)" | Set packed flags. |
| \ref StFcsCollection::print "print(option)" | Print summary (option ≥ 1 = points, ≥ 2 = clusters, ≥ 3 = hits). |

\section fcs_example Usage Example

\code{.cpp}
#include "StEvent/StFcsCollection.h"
#include "StEvent/StFcsHit.h"
#include "StEnumerations.h"

StFcsCollection* fcsColl = event->fcsCollection();
if (!fcsColl || !fcsColl->isDataExist()) return;

// Iterate over ECAL-North photon points
for (unsigned int i = 0; i < fcsColl->numberOfPoints(kFcsEcalNorthDetId); ++i) {
    StFcsPoint* pt = fcsColl->points(kFcsEcalNorthDetId)[i];
    // use pt ...
}

// Add a new hit (heap-allocated; ownership transfers to the collection)
StFcsHit* h = new StFcsHit();
fcsColl->addHit(kFcsHcalSouthDetId, h);
\endcode
*/
